tures  not  used for orientation  are present holding together a transected part of the  specimen along the inferior margin  The specimen is sectioned at 3mm  intervals from lateral to medial revealing 90  of the specimen to be composed  of rubbery white fibrous tissue  without firm foci suggestive of invasive  carcinoma  and the remaining 10  being adipose tissue  The fibrous tissue  extends to all but the superior and lateral margins  The specimen is entirely  submitted   Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue  11 frags  ESS  Part two  labeled   2   consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue  3 5 x REMOVED_DATE  x 0 9cm   which is received in pathology already inked per pathology protocol  for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue  superior    red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  The specimen is also  received with a specimen radiograph which is reported as clip in specimen  The  specimen is serially sectioned at 3mm intervals from lateral to medial  revealing a specimen which is completely composed of soft rubbery white fibrous  tissue with no firm areas to suggest invasive carcinoma  The clip is  identified within the specimen near the inferior margin  submitted in cassette  8   The specimen is entirely submitted   Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue  11 frags  ESS  eab  Reports to  LESNIKOSKI  BETH ANN M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  SURGICAL MARGIN   report_end  , no_ILC.
